// Rule: [T1574.001] Mirage Kitten - Appvshnotify Sspicli Sideloading
// MITRE ATT&CK: T1574.001
// Classification: Production candidate
// Status: Untested implementation sketch
// Primary platform: Microsoft Defender XDR
// Required telemetry: DeviceImageLoadEvents
// Purpose: Behavioral detection for AppVShNotify loading a co-located SspiCli module outside the Windows directory.
// Logic: Evaluate DeviceImageLoadEvents for appvshnotify sspicli sideloading using the existing source-derived conditions while preserving projected investigation context.
// A match proves: The documented host binary loaded a same-directory SspiCli.dll from a non-Windows path and requires immediate file and process validation.
// A match does not prove: Malicious DLL contents, successful C2, operator activity, data theft or Mirage Kitten attribution.
// Expected false positives: authorized administration, approved software, testing, or benign artifact collisions.
// Coverage limits: local schema, field population, retention, collection scope, and attacker variation require validation.
// Evidence claims: C001, C002, C003
//
// Title: AppVShNotify loads co-located SspiCli outside the Windows directory
// Platform: Microsoft Defender XDR Advanced Hunting
// Status: Production candidate - Untested implementation sketch
// Confidence: Medium
// Telemetry prerequisite: Microsoft Defender for Endpoint; DeviceImageLoadEvents
// Evidence: Kaspersky observed NightLedger masquerading as SspiCli.dll and using
// AppVShNotify.exe for DLL search-order hijacking. The malicious DLL is co-located
// with the legitimate executable. The non-Windows-path restriction is an analyst
// assumption intended to reduce servicing and operating-system overlap.
DeviceImageLoadEvents
| where InitiatingProcessFileName =~ "AppVShNotify.exe"
| where FileName =~ "SspiCli.dll"
| where FolderPath =~ InitiatingProcessFolderPath
| where not(InitiatingProcessFolderPath startswith @"C:\Windows\")
| project
    Timestamp,
    DeviceId,
    DeviceName,
    InitiatingProcessAccountName,
    InitiatingProcessFolderPath,
    InitiatingProcessCommandLine,
    InitiatingProcessSHA1,
    FolderPath,
    FileName,
    SHA1,
    ReportId
| order by Timestamp desc
